{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123296-house-bjornaer-and-the-heartbeast","id":1123296,"title":"House Bjornaer and the Heartbeast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-31T20:45:43-07:00","id":1123296,"title":"House Bjornaer and the Heartbeast","content":"Those familiar with Mage know that the Order of Hermes is co-opted by the game Ars Magica, which uses the original Houses in its own medieval setting. One of those houses is House Bjornaer, a Mystery Cult that filters traditional Germanic paganism through a Hermetic lens. And the House's defining feature is that each member has gone through a ritual to awaken their &quot;Heartbeast&quot;, a manifestation of the soul as a result of ancient animal ancestry. It allows the Bjornaer to change, at will, into a particular kind of animal; because the animal form is just as much a part of the magus as their human form, it requires no spell, and when transformed they appear to all mundane and magical senses as being that animal.<br /> <br /> Naturally, it got me wondering if this feature could be ported to Mage: The Ascension. True, House Bjornaer isn't really a thing in the modern Order of Hermes; most of them moved over to the Verbana when that Tradition formed, leaving maybe two or three stubborn Hermetic loyalists to hang out in House Ex Misc. But that doesn't mean the knowledge for how to awaken the Heartbeast need be lost. Germanic Verbana might carry the secret, and those Hermetic outliers certainly would (being scholars, after all). So, why not?<br /> <br /> I'm imagining it either as a Merit, or as a particular kind of mystic Enhancement, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1080786-non-tech-biotech-and-traditionalist-enhancements\">like I've discussed before on this forum</a>. The latter is straightforward enough - an inborn Life 4 Rote that turns the Mage into a specific beast - so I don't need to go into any great detail about it. As such, I'll focus on the Merit.<br /> <br /> The Merit would designate one animal that the mage can just change into, at will. Takes a turn to pull off, and we'll be strict and say the character can't do anything besides transform (and maybe move). It's not stepping on the toes of any Werewolf or other shapechanger, because it only gives the complete transformation. No rapid healing or soak, no innate connection to the spirit world or ability to step sideways, and no shifting into a form in between shapes (you're either a human or an animal, not a man-animal/manimal). All those features need to be accomplished with additional Merits or with Sphere magick. Changing forms is the entire package. It may or may not cause Paradox, depending on whether you think the Heartbeast is a static enough part of the character's Pattern to make it Coincidental, or if you think it's just too potent to make free. This would also factor into how expensive the Merit is; at most, I'd say 7 points.<br /> <br /> How the character got the Merit could vary by backstory. The obvious is that the character underwent the ritual performed by Bjornaer-descended mages (probably some crazy strong spell with multiple rank 5 Spheres involved; Life 5 + Prime 3/4 + Spirit 5, or something). Another is that they had Bjornaer ancestors, so the tendency towards a Heartbeast traveled down the line. Another is that they were a shapechanger kinfolk (so they take that Merit too), and their Heartbeast represented some kind of freak, stilted version of the First Change. Like something went wrong, or the kinfolk wanted to change so badly they Awakened and Wild Magicked themselves into an altered spiritual makeup that allowed the change.<br /> <br /> There might be added benefits and downsides to having a Heartbeast. The aforementioned Shapechangers might see the mage as an abomination or shameful, half-formed wretch, and either shun them, or want to destroy them. Having one kind of animal being so significant to the mage's very being could make emulating that beast with Life easier, while taking on traits of animals directly contrary to that Heartbeast would be harder. A mage with a wolf Heartbeast could grow a wolf's claws with magick at -1 difficulty, perhaps, while a hare's ears would be +1 (because a rabbit is a prey animal). And of course, most animals lack the ability to employ certain Instruments, limiting a mage's options while in the form of the Heartbeast. That wolf from earlier could make eye contact well enough, but not mutter a spell, make hand gestures, use a wand, or ride a broom. At least, not well enough that their Focus would allow it. A Heartbeast mage would need to rely on certain Instruments, or upon Effects cast before the transformation. (Ars Magica, for comparison, makes all Hermetic spells require verbal and somatic components (unless it didn't), so casting them in Heartbeast mode was usually impossible (unless it wasn't).).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T21:34:02-07:00","id":1123307,"title":"","content":"Isn't this litterally what the background Blessing is meant to cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:53:54-07:00","id":1123322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123296-house-bjornaer-and-the-heartbeast?p=1123307#post1123307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this litterally what the background Blessing is meant to cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it. It's basically a Life 4 Effect, so it would be Blessing 4. The one giving the blessing, in this case, would probably be the Bjornaer Masters who performed the Ritual of Twelve Years (the spell in Ars Magica) on the character, since Guide to the Traditions does say that groups of Mages can serve that function. Or maybe Gaia, if the character is a shapechanger kinfolk who the spirit of nature took pity on. Or some ancient animal ancestor. Or a Totem. And you could take Conditional Magic as a Flaw, so they have a greater difficulty transforming (whole or in part) into beasts contrary to the Heartbeast. And having the Heartbeast be tied to a Background rather than a Merit would leave more room for other Merits, like Shapechanger Kin.<br /> <br /> There are problems to this method, though. If you're using M20, you obviously can't replicate the power using that version of Blessing. One of the rules of that version is that the benefit can't appear overtly supernatural. And transforming into a robin qualifies. M20 also has another way to justify internal powers: the aforementioned Enhancements, which I've argued should be open to mystic Paradigms. On another note, you can't have your character's Heartbeast be a result of Wild Magick if we're using Blessing, since you have no patron save yourself. Doubt that counts.<br /> <br /> Plus, one of the points of having the Heartbeast is that it doesn't pop up on magical senses. A mage in Heartbeast form will look, for all intents and purposes, like a typical example of its kind, right down to the Pattern. If we want to replicate the Heartbeast from Ars Magica in as many was as possible, just Blessing wouldn't cut it. We'd need a Merit all on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T23:20:48-07:00","id":1123325,"title":"","content":"I'm more willing to go with the Revised version of Blessing where it basically is &quot;Enhancements for Mystics&quot; since &quot;Wonder tattoo&quot; exists which is pretty much hitting that hard. Revised even had naturally occuring wonders.<br /> <br /> On the other hand this seems to be a technique that was specific to the Bjorner should people not following their methods be able to do it, it seemed very close to a unique benny of their faction. ON the third hand(the hand grown with science) the fact that it can no longer be replicated easily and readily can show how much the Consensus has shifted. The features no longer available become so because of paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}